# Strings to remove from every commit. One pair per line: old<TAB>new
#
# Copy this to `scripts/scrub-tokens.txt` and fill in real values. That file is
# gitignored, because it necessarily contains exactly the data being removed —
# committing it would undo the point of the exercise.
#
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. Longer strings are applied first, so
# a token containing another is replaced whole.
#
# Choose replacements that keep each file's shape plausible: a path segment
# stays a path segment, a title stays a title, a name stays a name. History
# should read as if the personal detail was never there, not as if a redaction
# tool ran over it.
#
# Only distinctive strings belong here — ones safe to replace *anywhere* in any
# file. Generic patterns (home directories, identifier shapes) are already
# handled in code and need no entry. A common English word here would corrupt
# unrelated text in every commit.

alice	example
Superwidget	example-project
ab1234-project-partner	example-service
Some Course Title	example-docs
COURSE1234	example-api
